On the 选汉字 rung the only input is the option buttons, and a click on one neither started
the clock nor cleared a pause: the learner picked a wrong hanzi, saw it flash red, picked
again, and all the while the header read 按任意键开始 and the clock 00:00, until the right pick
passed the word and finishWord set running (b-ladder.cjs: wrong pick at 0.5 s, clock still
00:00 two seconds later). After the pause button the first pick graded the word on a card
that still said it was paused, with the same silent resume at the pass. 3d36559 gave the
打拼音 box an onResume on every change; the pick handler calls the same callback, so the clock
runs from the learner's first move and a pick after a pause resumes it openly. 认读 is
unchanged: its only move is the pass itself, which starts the clock already.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ZhSteps.tsx | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ZhSteps.tsx b/src/ZhSteps.tsx
index f8931ac..7c50344 100644
--- a/src/ZhSteps.tsx
+++ b/src/ZhSteps.tsx
@@ -255,6 +255,10 @@ export function ZhSteps({ step, word, plain, pool, uiLang, active, onPass, onSki
           className={picked === o ? (o === word ? "ok" : "no") : ""}
           onClick={() => {
             if (picked === word) return;
+            // a pick is the learner's first move on the card: the clock starts (or resumes after a
+            // pause) as a key into the pinyin box does — the header used to say 按任意键开始 and the
+            // clock to read 00:00 through every wrong pick until the right one passed the word
+            onResume();
             setPicked(o);
             if (o === word) { onSpeak(); onPass(); }
             else { onMiss(); setTimeout(() => setPicked(null), 420); }
